### Delicias da Lu - API Test Requests
### Base URL for all requests
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080/v1
@timestamp = {{$timestamp}}

### ============================================
### ERROR ENDPOINT - TYPE REQUESTS
### ============================================

### Get Error Type: not-found
GET {{baseUrl}}/error?filter=type&identifier=not-found

### Get Error Type: invalid-type
GET {{baseUrl}}/error?filter=type&identifier=invalid-type

### Get Error Type: invalid-credentials
GET {{baseUrl}}/error?filter=type&identifier=invalid-credentials

### Get Error Type: invalid-token
GET {{baseUrl}}/error?filter=type&identifier=invalid-token

### Get Error Type: unauthorized
GET {{baseUrl}}/error?filter=type&identifier=unauthorized

### Get Error Type: type-not-found
GET {{baseUrl}}/error?filter=type&identifier=type-not-found

### Get Error Type: instance-not-found
GET {{baseUrl}}/error?filter=type&identifier=instance-not-found

### Get Error Type: invalidDocumentLenght
GET {{baseUrl}}/error?filter=type&identifier=invalidDocumentLenght

### Get Error Type: invalidFilter
GET {{baseUrl}}/error?filter=type&identifier=invalidFilter

### Get Error Type: unexpectedUnhandledError
GET {{baseUrl}}/error?filter=type&identifier=unexpectedUnhandledError

### ============================================
### ERROR ENDPOINT - INSTANCE REQUESTS
### ============================================

### Get Error Instance by Trace ID (example - replace with actual trace ID)
### After running a request that generates an error, copy the X-Trace-Id from response header
GET {{baseUrl}}/error?filter=instance&identifier=a1b2c3d4e5f6g7h8

### ============================================
### AUTH ENDPOINTS - For generating errors
### ============================================

### Health Check (baseline)
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### Login with invalid credentials (generates error)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "invalid_user",
  "password": "wrong_password"
}

### Login with valid credentials
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "juliosshoji",
  "password": "password123"
}

### Refresh Token (no token - generates unauthorized error)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh-token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refresh_token": "invalid_token"
}

### ============================================
### MENU ENDPOINTS - For testing trace propagation
### ============================================

### Get All Menu Items
GET {{baseUrl}}/menu/items

### Get Menu Item with invalid ID (generates not-found error)
GET {{baseUrl}}/menu/items/invalid-id-12345

### Get Menu Item with valid ID (replace with actual ID)
GET {{baseUrl}}/menu/items/actual-menu-item-id

### Create Menu Item (with auth token)
POST {{baseUrl}}/menu/items
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE

{
  "name": "Chocolate Cake",
  "description": "Rich chocolate cake with ganache",
  "price": 45.99,
  "category": "bolos",
  "active": true
}

### ============================================
### CAKE BUILDER ENDPOINTS
### ============================================

### Get Massa (Dough) Components
GET {{baseUrl}}/cakebuilder/massa

### Get Recheio (Filling) Components
GET {{baseUrl}}/cakebuilder/recheio

### Get Cobertura (Topping) Components
GET {{baseUrl}}/cakebuilder/cobertura

### Get Decoracao (Decoration) Components
GET {{baseUrl}}/cakebuilder/decoracao

### Get Cake Component with invalid ID (generates not-found error)
GET {{baseUrl}}/cakebuilder/massa/invalid-component-id

### ============================================
### ORDER ENDPOINTS
### ============================================

### List All Orders
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders

### Get Order by ID (replace with actual order ID)
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders/order-id-12345

### Get Order with invalid ID (generates not-found error)
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders/invalid-order-id-99999

### Create Order
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE

{
  "customer_name": "João Silva",
  "customer_phone": "11999999999",
  "customer_email": "joao@example.com",
  "items": [
    {
      "menu_item_id": "chocolate-cake-001",
      "quantity": 1,
      "unit_price": 45.99
    }
  ],
  "delivery_date": "2026-06-15T14:00:00Z",
  "special_instructions": "Sem amendoim - alérgico"
}

### ============================================
### SYSTEM ENDPOINTS
### ============================================

### Health Check
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### Get Error Type Documentation (type filter)
GET {{baseUrl}}/error?filter=type&identifier=not-found

### Get Error Instance Documentation (instance filter with trace ID)
### Note: Replace trace-id-example with actual trace ID from error response
GET {{baseUrl}}/error?filter=instance&identifier=trace-id-example

### Get Error with invalid filter (generates error)
GET {{baseUrl}}/error?filter=invalid&identifier=something

### Get Error with missing identifier (generates error)
GET {{baseUrl}}/error?filter=type

### Get Error Type that doesn't exist (generates type-not-found error)
GET {{baseUrl}}/error?filter=type&identifier=non-existent-error-type

### ============================================
### CONTACT ENDPOINTS
### ============================================

### Get Contact Information
GET {{baseUrl}}/contacts

### Update Contact Information
PUT {{baseUrl}}/contacts
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE

{
  "phone": "1133334444",
  "email": "contact@deliciasdalui.com.br",
  "address": "Rua das Flores, 123",
  "instagram": "@deliciasdalui",
  "whatsapp": "11988887777"
}

### ============================================
### CONFIG ENDPOINTS
### ============================================

### Get Site Configuration (Public View)
GET {{baseUrl}}/config

### Update Site Configuration (Admin Only)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/config
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE

{
  "site_title": "Delícias da Lui",
  "maintenance_mode": false,
  "max_orders_per_day": 50
}

### ============================================
### TRACE ID TESTING
### ============================================

### Send request with custom Trace ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/menu/items
X-Trace-Id: custom-trace-001

### Send request with custom Trace ID to error endpoint
GET {{baseUrl}}/error?filter=type&identifier=not-found
X-Trace-Id: custom-trace-error-001

### ============================================
### ERROR GENERATION SCENARIOS
### ============================================

### Scenario 1: Generate invalid-credentials error
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "admin",
  "password": "wrongpassword"
}

### Scenario 2: Generate unauthorized error (no token)
GET {{baseUrl}}/menu/items
Authorization: 

### Scenario 3: Generate invalid-token error
GET {{baseUrl}}/menu/items
Authorization: Bearer invalid.token.here

### Scenario 4: Generate not-found error
GET {{baseUrl}}/menu/items/nonexistent-item-id

### Scenario 5: Generate invalidDocumentLenght error (CPF/CNPJ validation)
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Test User",
  "document": "123"
}

### ============================================
### WORKFLOW: Complete Error Tracking
### ============================================

### Step 1: Trigger an error (login with wrong password)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "admin",
  "password": "wrong"
}

### Copy X-Trace-Id from response header and use in Step 2

### Step 2: Query error instance documentation
### GET {{baseUrl}}/error?filter=instance&identifier={TRACE_ID_FROM_STEP_1}

### Step 3: Query error type documentation
GET {{baseUrl}}/error?filter=type&identifier=invalid-credentials

### ============================================
### NOTES FOR TESTING
### ============================================
### 1. Replace YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE with actual token from login endpoint
### 2. After each error request, note the X-Trace-Id from response header
### 3. Use that trace ID to fetch the error instance documentation
### 4. Verify logs include trace_id, user_id, caller information
### 5. Check Firestore collections:
###    - delicias-da-lu-service/types/{error-identifier}
###    - delicias-da-lu-service/instances/{trace-id}
